{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>A woman when she conceives</b> — juxtaposed with 'and you shall sanctify yourselves' (Leviticus 11:44) to 'a woman when she conceives,' teaching that one must sanctify himself at the time of relations. And it is written above, 'do not make yourselves abominable' (Leviticus 11:43). And we derive from this that one should not delay his emissions (i.e., withhold seed). A hint: one who comes from the privy should not lie with his wife immediately." "<b>to distinguish between the unclean and the clean</b> — and juxtaposed to 'a woman when she conceives,' teaching that one must wait three months to distinguish between seed and seed, and to refrain from relations with her near her period." "<b>Male</b> — in gematria: ברכה (blessing)." "<b>And she is unclean seven days</b> — and likewise seven days of mourning; corresponding to what she experiences, so it proceeds."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:15.635237179Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}